meta {
  type: collection
}

auth {
  mode: none
}

headers {
  Accept: application/json
}

docs {
  Select Local and copy .env.example to .env before signing in.
  Public and authentication requests send no bearer token. Player and Admin
  folders inherit their own bearer token. Login tokens and captured IDs stay
  in runtime variables; scripts never persist credentials to environment files.

  Run folders in numbered order for the complete scenario. Registration creates
  a disposable player and signs in as that player for the rest of the run.
  Admin cleanup deletes that account. Do not run the scenario in parallel.
  Global reset and Firebase authentication are optional; see their Docs tabs.
  See README.md for setup, endpoint criteria, and running on a temporary database.
}
